    "https://www.ufv.ca/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Donors Calendar myUFV myClass Library Careers Toggle navigation UFV.ca Information For Alumni Current Students Donors Future Students International Tools Academic Calendar Library myUFV myClass Programs Admissions Student Services Research News Events About UFV We are looking for great people like you. UFV is a community of great people: faculty and staff who want to support students, engage with the community, and change the world with ground-breaking research. Ready to inspire, mentor, and grow? Join the team and help shape the future. Current opportunities at UFV Current opportunities at UFV Careers UFV / Careers Explore engaging job opportunities in the Fraser Valley The University of the Fraser Valley offers engaging career opportunities in a supportive, friendly culture that values integrity, inclusivity, community and excellence. In an ideal location near Vancouver, you'll experience the beauty and vibrancy of the Fraser Valley, one of the fastest-growing communities in British Columbia. At UFV, you can balance career aspirations without sacrificing personal pursuits. Come join us! Living into our mission We work together to engage learners, transform lives, and build community. It's our vision for UFV to be known as a gathering place for learners, leaders, and seekers — a Íyáqáwtxw —  House of Transformation for everyone at UFV. Outstanding benefits package Comprehensive total compensation package which includes salary, group benefits, pension plans, and many other programs. A uniquely supportive culture UFV is a community of individuals with diverse abilities, backgrounds and identities, each contributing to the richness of our workplace. We foster a climate of collaboration, genuine camaraderie and mutual respect. Committed to your development Generous PD funds, workplace learning opportunities, and a dedicated Teaching & Learning Centre to help you learn and grow. See job postings Living into our mission Dr. Christine Slavik, Associate Professor Read Christine's story Working here: exciting and productive Dr. Edward Akuffo, Associate Professor Read Edward's story Supporting personal transformation Lorna Peters, Teaching & Learning Specialist Read Lorna's story Engaging learners, transforming lives, and building community Dr. Christine Slavik Associate Professor – Child, Youth and Family Studies For me, UFV is unique in the way we connect to support each other. We actually live into our mission of engaging learners, transforming lives, and building community. UFV has a strong sense of community and brings in the larger community to campus. Bring your whole self to this community, your passion, your ideas. Join committees, get involved, inspire and spark the next stage of this incredible place. Find your career at UFV Transformation, Indigenization, reconciliation Lorna Peters Teaching and Learning Specialist (Indigenization) I started as a student in the early 1990s, and always knew that I wanted to work at UFV when I was done my graduate degree. I wanted to give back to Indigenous peoples and the greater community, and UFV is a great place to support that. In my role as a Teaching and Learning specialist for Indigenization, I work with faculty and staff who want to make a difference for Indigenous people, community and students. Seeing the transformation that folks go through in their own work of decolonization, indigenization, and reconciliation is exceptionally rewarding. Find your career at UFV Supporting staff initiatives and leadership skills Dr. Edward Akuffo Associate Professor and Head, Political Science As a smaller university, UFV offers a great opportunity to work with students, faculty, staff, and administrators very closely. This work culture is priceless. UFV has a strong sense of community and brings in the larger community to campus. UFV strongly supports staff initiatives and development of leadership skills.  This entire relationship makes working here exciting and productive. You'll be joining an ambitious and result oriented students, faculty, staff, and administration who take delight in academic excellence. Find your career at UFV BC Top Employer UFV has been named a Top Employer in BC for the eleventh year in a row. Learn more about UFV's Top Employer recognition Helpful links Compensation and incentives Learn more about UFV's outstanding salary and benefits package. How to apply Guidance for creating your UFV profile and what to expect during the application process. Contact UFV Careers Connect with our HR careers team 1-604-854-4554 hrinfo@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Directory Emergency contacts IT Service Desk Reset your password Safety & Security myUFV Current Students Academic Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Schedule of classes myClass CIVL Radio About us UFV Changemaking Accessible UFV EDI & Human Rights Office Open Education Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us University of the Fraser Valley 33844 King Road , Abbotsford, BC Canada V2S 7M8 604-504-7441 The University of the Fraser Valley is situated in the traditional territory of the Stó:lō peoples. The Stó:lō have an intrinsic relationship with what they refer to as S'olh Téméxw (Our Sacred Land); therefore, we express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in this territory. Copyright · Privacy · Sitemap · Feedback Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question"
    }
  },
